            <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41893-024-01444-1">doi:10.1038/s41893-024-01444-1</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            Subsequent evidence (2025 review; 2026 research): radical flank
            effects can be positive or negative depending on political context,
            audience characteristics and how the protest is perceived.
          </li>
          <li>
            “Personal climate actions do not crowd out collective action and
            policy support: longitudinal evidence.” <i>npj Climate Action</i>
            (2026). N = 2,778, Australian survey, four annual waves 2021–2024.
            <span class="refnote">Defensible finding: personal action does not crowd out collective action. No systematic year-to-year spillover was found.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            Fuchs, D. et al. / EU 1.5° Lifestyles Consortium (2026). “Enabling
            1.5 °C lifestyles in Europe: lifestyle options and structural change
            for transformation.”
            <i>Sustainability: Science, Practice and Policy</i>, 22(1).
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/15487733.2026.2657131">doi:10.1080/15487733.2026.2657131</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            “The potential of individuals to reduce greenhouse gas emissions
            through their own actions: a case of a suburb in Finland.”
            <i>Discover Sustainability</i> (2024).
            <span class="refnote">Local case study; not extrapolated as a universal measurement.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            BP, “Beyond Petroleum” campaign and online carbon footprint
            calculator (2004), developed with Ogilvy. See also 2024 academic
            literature on carbon-footprint calculators, and Bundeszentrale für
            politische Bildung, “Klimaschutz im Alltag.”
            <span class="refnote">BP did not invent the concept — the ecological footprint dates from the 1990s — but played an important role in popularising the personal carbon footprint.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <p class="origin">
          This essay was written in Spanish and translated by the author.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="book-cta" aria-label="About the book">
      <h2>{book.title}</h2>
      <p>
        Over 100 specific actions across home energy, water, food, transport and
        community — paired with grounding practices for the days when
        eco-anxiety takes over. Short by design.
      </p>
      {amazon && (
        <p class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-amazon" href={amazon.url} rel="noopener">
            Get the book on Amazon
          </a>
        </p>
      )}
    </aside>

    <p class="back-link">
      <a href="/blog/">&larr; All essays in {blog.name}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

